## Scope and method

The 16-scalar per-row state is `Q1_FEATURES`, declared at
[state.py:29-46](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py:29)
and assembled into `q1_state` at
[state.py:397-413](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py:403).
It is the **entire** input of the C1 route and **half of each member's** input to
the C3 route:

```python
def _route_state(row: SourceRow, route: Route) -> tuple[float, ...]:
    if route == "C1":  return row.q1_state
    if route == "C2":  return row.q2_state
    return (*row.q1_state, *row.q2_state)
```

[learner.py:167-172](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:167);
C3 additionally carries `selected_q1_row` and `incumbent_q1_row` per coalition
member ([coalitions.py:41-42](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/coalitions.py:41),
[coalitions.py:70-71](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/coalitions.py:70)).
Seven of the 16 slots reappear inside the 22-slot `q2_state` that C2 consumes, so
a dead Q1 slot is not confined to C1.

Source of truth read for this audit: `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws` at commit
`857b4bd`. Measurement ran against a copy at
`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coverage-ws/src-copy` (`src/`, `scripts/`, the probe engine,
and the four contract documents the launch digest hashes), under
`/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python` (3.13.3), `nice -n 15`, all BLAS
thread counts pinned to 1, never more than four concurrent processes. The pilot
tree and the handover venv were not modified.

One deliberate in-process deviation, stated because Part B depends on it: to
obtain a normal-path row for the *same* anchor as a fallback row, the diagnostic
process sets `PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK = False` on its own imported module
object for the duration of one call. The file on disk is byte-identical
throughout, and this is the only way the requested both-ways diff can exist at
all, since the flag is the dispatch condition.

## Part A — slot census

### Basis

Two independent row sets, both from real tapes built by the sealed v025 pilot
tape constructor (`build_world_tape(domain=..., provider=LegacyWorldProvider(
role="pilot-source"), steps=33, start_time_s=0.0)`, as used at
[run_v025_pilot_c3.py:973](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:973)):

| Row set | Rows | Anchors | Worlds | Carriers |
|---|---:|---:|---|---|
| **S — shipped pilot source corpus** (primary) | **176,223** | 180 | `V025_PROBE/world/1`, `V025_PROBE/world/2` | all 3 |
| **R — regenerated here** (reproduction) | **87,997** | 90 | `V025_PROBE/world/1` | all 3 |

Row set R regenerated world 1 from scratch through the same entry point and
produced **exactly 87,997 rows, the same count the production manifest records
for that world**, with the same 16-slot structure. Every structural conclusion
below holds identically in both row sets; the tables quote row set S, because
those are the rows a training run would actually load.

All figures are in the slots' declared physical units. The learner consumes
`q1_state[i] = raw[i] / scale[i]` with a fixed positive per-slot scale
([state.py:29-46](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py:29)),
so that diagonal positive rescaling changes no distinct-value count, no
correlation, no R², and no rank. Where the scaling matters — conditioning — both
are reported.

